# Force LF line endings on checkout for embedded Go template files,
# regardless of the checking-out machine's platform or core.autocrlf
# setting. These files are read via `//go:embed` (e.g.
# internal/adapter/backend/{chi,gin,...}/templates/*.tmpl) and their
# rendered output is asserted against byte-for-byte in tests such as
# TestBackendAdapters_Dockerizable (internal/adapter/adapter_test.go). Git
# for Windows commonly defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout for anything it classifies as text — silently breaking
# those exact-content assertions (go:chi and go:gin failing on
# windows-latest CI, but not other backend adapters, was traced to this).
# `text eol=lf` keeps normal diffing/text handling but pins the checked-out
# line ending to LF on every platform.
*.tmpl text eol=lf
